# Review package: ticket 03, 9ea7bdd..496eb962e1c631e11a9383347a9d2bfd381fa3f6

## Commits
### 496eb96
Pin the just-over-pace warning and take limitWords' flags as options

limitWords takes { classic, overPace } in place of two positional booleans. A new test warns of a 7d at r 1.03, which the hover reads as on pace. The paused 5h test shares one now with startWithLimits.

### 0dd10c2
Make the run-out warning speak the explanation's sentence

The warning reads each limit through limitOf as its tag does, so a refused limit and a paused 5h do not warn, and shows when a limit reaches its target before it resets, even if that moment has passed. Its text is limitWords' over-pace sentence, which names the 7d for a bounded 5h and the reset by its clock time. explainLine reads one live snapshot for the warning and the explanations.

The README, the limit_forecast description and the glossary say target, not 100%.


